export const meta = {
  name: 'agent-docs-compat-research',
  description: 'Research how each major AI coding agent (Codex, Claude, opencode, Cursor, Copilot, Gemini, Windsurf, Aider, Cline) discovers project instructions, the AGENTS.md standard, and CONTRACT.md conventions — to plan making the Orva repo agent-agnostic',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Research', detail: 'one read-only agent per AI-tool cluster + standards' },
    { title: 'Synthesize', detail: 'gap analysis + compatibility matrix + recommendation' },
  ],
}

const READONLY = `IMPORTANT: This is READ-ONLY research inside a plan-mode session. Do NOT edit, create, or delete any files. Use WebSearch/WebFetch (and Read/Bash for repo facts) only.
Prefer PRIMARY sources: each tool's official docs / GitHub repo / the agents.md standard site. For each claim note the source. Where docs are ambiguous or changed recently, say so. Today is 2026; verify current behavior, not stale blog posts.
Your output is structured data for a synthesis step, not a human message.`

const TOOL_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    tools: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        properties: {
          tool: { type: 'string', description: 'e.g. "OpenAI Codex CLI"' },
          discoveryFiles: {
            type: 'array',
            items: { type: 'string' },
            description: 'Exact filenames/paths it reads for project instructions, in precedence order (e.g. AGENTS.md, .cursor/rules/*.mdc, .github/copilot-instructions.md)',
          },
          nestedSupport: { type: 'string', description: 'Does it read instruction files in SUBDIRECTORIES (nested/hierarchical merge)? yes/no/partial + how (e.g. merges closest dir upward).' },
          honorsAgentsMd: { type: 'string', description: 'Does it natively read AGENTS.md? yes/no/via-config/planned' },
          format: { type: 'string', description: 'Plain markdown? frontmatter with globs? JSON config? size limits / @import support?' },
          globalConfig: { type: 'string', description: 'User/global config location if any (~/.codex, ~/.claude, etc.)' },
          notes: { type: 'string', description: 'Gotchas: precedence, symlink handling, whether it follows symlinks, recent changes, whether a symlink of AGENTS.md->CLAUDE.md works for it.' },
          orvaRecommendation: { type: 'string', description: 'Concretely, what file(s) should the Orva repo add so THIS tool gets full context (root + subdirs).' },
          sources: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
        },
        required: ['tool', 'discoveryFiles', 'nestedSupport', 'honorsAgentsMd', 'orvaRecommendation'],
      },
    },
    extraFindings: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' }, description: 'Anything important outside the per-tool rows (standards status, symlink caveats, single-source-of-truth strategies).' },
  },
  required: ['tools'],
}

phase('Research')

const RESEARCH = [
  {
    key: 'codebase',
    schema: {
      type: 'object',
      properties: {
        currentState: { type: 'string', description: 'Exact inventory: every CLAUDE.md path, the AGENTS.md symlink, any agent-config files, docs/CONTRIBUTING.md, .gitignore entries for agent artifacts.' },
        claudeMdStructure: { type: 'string', description: 'What the root + nested CLAUDE.md files actually contain (sections, style, how build/test/gotchas are expressed). Read root CLAUDE.md + backend/CLAUDE.md + cli/CLAUDE.md fully.' },
        gaps: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' }, description: 'Concrete gaps for multi-agent use, grounded in the file inventory.' },
        contractCandidates: { type: 'string', description: 'What canonical operational facts (build/test/lint commands, CI gates, sync invariants, gotchas) are scattered across the CLAUDE.md set and could be consolidated into a CONTRACT.md.' },
      },
      required: ['currentState', 'gaps'],
    },
    prompt: `${READONLY}

Map the Orva repo (/home/dev/Orva) agent-documentation state precisely. Run git ls-files + find for: all CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md/GEMINI.md/.cursor/.github/copilot-instructions.md/.clinerules/.windsurfrules/opencode.json/CONVENTIONS.md/CONTRACT.md, and which are symlinks (readlink). Read the ROOT CLAUDE.md, backend/CLAUDE.md, and cli/CLAUDE.md fully to understand structure/quality/style. Check .gitignore for any agent-artifact entries. Note the repo layout (backend/ cli/ frontend/ docs/ scripts/ test/ test/e2e/ each has a CLAUDE.md). Identify the gaps for making this usable by ANY AI agent, and what operational facts (build/test/lint, CI gates, docs-embed sync, release policy, gotchas) could form a canonical CONTRACT.md.`,
  },
  {
    key: 'codex-standard',
    schema: TOOL_SCHEMA,
    prompt: `${READONLY}

Cover: (1) OpenAI Codex — both the Codex CLI and Codex cloud/IDE — how it discovers project instructions (AGENTS.md), whether it MERGES nested AGENTS.md hierarchically (root + subdir + cwd), precedence with ~/.codex/ global config and any legacy codex.md, size limits. (2) The AGENTS.md OPEN STANDARD (agents.md): what it is, who maintains it, which tools have officially adopted it, whether the standard specifies nested/monorepo AGENTS.md, and its relationship to CLAUDE.md. For each, does a symlink AGENTS.md->CLAUDE.md work, and is nested AGENTS.md read? Return per-tool rows + extraFindings on the standard's adoption/status.`,
  },
  {
    key: 'opencode-gemini',
    schema: TOOL_SCHEMA,
    prompt: `${READONLY}

Cover two tools: (1) opencode (github.com/sst/opencode / opencode.ai): instruction discovery — AGENTS.md, opencode.json "instructions", .opencode/, global ~/.config/opencode, nested support, precedence. (2) Google Gemini CLI (github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli): GEMINI.md discovery, hierarchical/nested loading (global ~/.gemini, project root, and subdirs up the tree), the configurable contextFileName, @import/@file includes, and whether it can be pointed at AGENTS.md. For each: does a symlink AGENTS.md->CLAUDE.md help, is nested honored, exact filenames. Return per-tool rows.`,
  },
  {
    key: 'cursor-copilot',
    schema: TOOL_SCHEMA,
    prompt: `${READONLY}

Cover two tools: (1) Cursor: current rules system — .cursor/rules/*.mdc with frontmatter (description, globs, alwaysApply), nested .cursor/rules in subdirectories, the legacy .cursorrules (deprecated?), and whether Cursor reads AGENTS.md. (2) GitHub Copilot (VS Code / copilot coding agent): .github/copilot-instructions.md (repo-wide), .github/instructions/*.instructions.md with applyTo globs (path-specific), AGENTS.md support status, and settings toggles. For each: nested/path-scoping support, format (frontmatter/globs), and exactly what Orva should add. Return per-tool rows.`,
  },
  {
    key: 'claude-others-contract',
    schema: TOOL_SCHEMA,
    prompt: `${READONLY}

Cover: (1) Claude Code — CLAUDE.md discovery: root + NESTED CLAUDE.md (does it auto-load subdir CLAUDE.md when working there, or only on-demand?), CLAUDE.local.md, ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md, and the @path import syntax; whether AGENTS.md is read natively (or only via symlink). (2) Windsurf: .windsurf/rules/*.md + legacy .windsurfrules, glob scoping. (3) Aider: CONVENTIONS.md convention + .aider.conf.yml read: entries; does it read AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md. (4) Cline / Roo Code: .clinerules (file or dir) / .roo/rules. Also research "CONTRACT.md" as a repo convention for AI agents (is it an established pattern? what do people put in an agent 'contract' — build/test commands, invariants, definition-of-done, guardrails?) and the best SINGLE-SOURCE-OF-TRUTH strategy across many agent files (symlink vs generated-from-one-source vs @import), including whether tools follow symlinks and how nested symlinks behave. Return per-tool rows + extraFindings covering CONTRACT.md conventions and the single-source strategy.`,
  },
]

const research = await parallel(
  RESEARCH.map(r => () => agent(r.prompt, { label: `research:${r.key}`, phase: 'Research', schema: r.schema }))
)
const good = research.filter(Boolean)
log(`${good.length}/${RESEARCH.length} research reports in`)

phase('Synthesize')
const digest = good.map((r, i) => `### ${RESEARCH[i]?.key || 'report'}\n${JSON.stringify(r, null, 1)}`).join('\n\n')

const SYN_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    compatibilityMatrix: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        properties: {
          tool: { type: 'string' },
          file: { type: 'string', description: 'the file(s) it reads' },
          nested: { type: 'string', description: 'nested-dir support: yes/no/partial' },
          orvaHasItToday: { type: 'string', description: 'what Orva currently provides for this tool (full/root-only/none)' },
          fix: { type: 'string', description: 'exact file(s) to add for full coverage' },
        },
        required: ['tool', 'file', 'nested', 'orvaHasItToday', 'fix'],
      },
    },
    theGap: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' }, description: 'Ranked list of the concrete gaps stopping any-agent use of this repo.' },
    recommendation: { type: 'string', description: 'The recommended single-source-of-truth strategy + exact set of files/symlinks/pointer-files to add, and how they stay in sync. Be concrete about nested AGENTS.md symlinks for the 7 subdirs.' },
    contractMd: { type: 'string', description: 'Recommended purpose + section outline for CONTRACT.md (what canonical operational contract it should hold, and how it differs from CLAUDE.md and docs/CONTRIBUTING.md).' },
    risks: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' }, description: 'Maintenance/drift risks and how to avoid them (e.g. symlinks on Windows checkouts, tools that ignore symlinks, duplicated content going stale).' },
  },
  required: ['compatibilityMatrix', 'theGap', 'recommendation', 'contractMd'],
}

const synthesis = await agent(`${READONLY}

Synthesize the research below into a concrete plan for making the Orva repo usable by ANY AI coding agent. Orva CURRENT STATE: root CLAUDE.md + AGENTS.md(symlink->CLAUDE.md); 7 nested CLAUDE.md (backend, cli, docs, frontend, scripts, test, test/e2e) with NO AGENTS.md; no .cursor/.github-copilot/GEMINI.md/.windsurf/opencode.json/.clinerules/CONVENTIONS.md; no CONTRACT.md; docs/CONTRIBUTING.md exists (human-facing).

Produce: a compatibility matrix (tool -> file, nested?, what Orva has today, exact fix), the ranked gap list, a recommended single-source-of-truth strategy (favor: keep CLAUDE.md as canonical, add AGENTS.md symlinks in each of the 7 subdirs, add thin per-tool pointer/config files that reference AGENTS.md, and a CONTRACT.md), the CONTRACT.md purpose+outline, and the drift/maintenance risks (esp. symlink portability). Respect that this is a self-hosted Go+Vue project whose docs are already high-quality and nested per-directory.

RESEARCH:
${digest}`, { label: 'synthesize', phase: 'Synthesize', schema: SYN_SCHEMA, effort: 'high' })

return { research: good, synthesis }

